  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsible and Inclusive Business Programme: Ukraine Business Compact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will strengthen the capacity of the UNGC Network in Ukraine and Government of Ukraine to promote the Ukraine Business Compact. This will give leading national and international businesses a platform to demonstrate their support for Responsible Business Conduct principles when engaging in Ukraine&#x2019;s recovery and reconstruction. The Governments of the UK and Ukraine co-hosted Ukraine Recovery Conference (URC23) in London in June 2023, which aimed to mobilize the international community to help secure Ukraine&#x2019;s long-term economic future, including helping Ukraine build back better, as a more resilient, greener, and more prosperous European nation. In particular, the URC23 placed emphasis on the strength and potential role of the private sector &#x2013; and the reforms required to drive investment &#x2013; as essential components of Ukraine&#x2019;s long-term recovery, in its drive to modernise, build a resilient and agile economy and emerge from war as a stronger and more prosperous state. The Ukraine Business Compact (UBC) was launched at URC23 to reinforce the business community&#x2019;s support for peace in in Ukraine and to set out mutual expectations for the success of recovery efforts. The Compact now has the co-secretariat of UNGCU and the Tony Blair Institute (TBI). It is crucial to actively engage and maintain the interest of international businesses both in identifying opportunities for companies to engage and invest in Ukraine, and also to support the government of Ukraine in reform implementation. Facilitating a constructive dialogue between the Government of Ukraine and the private sector is key to achieving this. The UBC is a readymade initiative to help facilitate dialogue between a broad range of private sector institutions and the government of Ukraine on these key issues.</narrative>
  </description>
